      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-09-21_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>BeLent:rm.</head>
        <p>BeLent:rm.</p>
        <p>J. B. Has, Teacher of Sandbuechel by lb,rschach, says : —" For many years my 'health was unsatisfactory. The malady SWITZBILLAND. showed itself in an alarming way, and it was found that! s.ffered from kidney disease, for which I employed Werner' Safe Cure, and after a thorough treatment was completely cured."</p>
        <p>7ai Sal Ram Missur, late Stationmaster of different Indian railways, resident of Village Khudra, District Futtehpore, N.W.P.. says :—" I was attacked by a fatal disease, dropsy. My whole body was filled with water, and kidneys refused to work. I tried various remedies, and talented and skilful European surgeons, and also native assistant surgeons, but all in vain. At !Asti was told my them to prepare for death. I then comtneneNl Warner's Safe Cure, and 20 bottles effeeted a com- plete cure."</p>
