        <p>Lot 7-59. High-class Second-hand Bedroom Suite,by Henry Ogden anct sons, Spanish Mahogany, consisting of 7ft, Spanish mahogany wardrobe, rich in colour, modern fittings, worth £75, for £3O. Pair of the handsomest stands to match In Manchester; dressing table 51t., washstand 4ft. 61n for 113/ guineas, worth £45. _ _</p>
        <p>Lot 791, A grand Bedroom Suite by Todd. In American walnut richly and profusely carved in bas relief ; a suite greatly admired. Wardrobe is a masterpiece of design and workmanship. beautifully finished inside with modern con- veniences. Dressing table is mounted with largeswing bevel- led mirror and jewel drawers. Washstand fitted with Carrara marble slab and back, three chairs, towel rail, and table de nult complete, a very charming and effective suite; price only 18 guineas; worth treble.—WOßSLßY'd. Lot 782. A similar Suite to Lot 791, same number of pieces for 10 guineas ; cost £36. WORSLEY S. A wonderful bar- gain. Lot 793. A genuine Sheraton Bedroom Suite, 6ft 81n.,00st £250, for £59 155. ; a real gem, worth seeing, first come, first served.—WORSLEY'S, Lot 891. American Ash Be Iroom Suite, cost £75, by Hud- son, £22. Similar to lot 863. Lot 897. Spanish MahoAany Wardrobe, break front, project- ing centre door, with full length crystal bevelled mirror, wings lined, bonnet drawers, four trays, three long drawers in centre, two large hanging eompartmente in the wiegs,very handsome, for £l5 15s. ; worth £5O. GREAT SALE OF PIANOS.</p>
        <p>WORSLEY'S "THE PANTHEON," GAYTHORN, _ MANCHMTER.</p>
        <p>MUSICAL CHAT.—The approach of the winter season is now causing flutters of excitement amongst young and old as to arrangements for musical enjoyment. The selection of a good musical instrument, in 99 cases out of a hundred, Is Pianoforte, and no more important purchase could be made. To possess an inferior inetrumnnt is to harhour a constant pest to yourself and a nuisance to everyone else ; to buy a good pianofnte is to make a good bid for personal comfort and enjo)ment, and a constant source of pleasure to all your friends. A word of advice on the selection of a Pianoforte may be acceptable; if so. then unless you can go to is high price. don't ourchase a new instrument, especially a ch-ap German. Going to o high price means purchasing a first-class pieno by aunt-class maker such as lirard, Steinway. Bro .d- -wood, Colla,d, Bechstein, Ibach, B insmead, and Kirkman. Worsley's, of Gaythorn, can remedy to h the highprice and the rrilseral le, cheapnew rubblsh,by submitting for salellifigh- class Second-band Pianofortes, by the above makers, at even- less cost than many inferior cheap Gerxians. livery Piano forte is warranted. and exchanged If not app raved Inspec- tion invited; please yourself whether you buy or not. Es- tablished 1841. Worsley's save 5 ) per cent in Pianos. Lot 131. Magnificent Rud Ibach, powerful; cost £BO, for £29. Lot 135. Splendid Broadwood, nearly new; cost £75, for 19 guineas. Lot 154. Really fine Collard and Collard Piano; cost LEO, for £2.5. Cheap. Lot 181. A Grand Cottage Plano, by Brinsmead ; cost £95. for £lB. _ .</p>
        <p>Lot 192. Magnificent Bboxised Piano, by Jauko ; cost £250, for £3O. Lot 220. A Handsome Rosewood Cott tge, by Chappel ; for £l2' cost £5O. Lot 223. The Handsomest and Best Pianoforte in Man- chester for £2B, being worth from £7O to £80; it Is by Erard, the noted maker, almost new, In splendid condition, full compass, 7 octaves, iron frame, with latest improvements. Guaranteed. Only requires inspection to effect a sale.— Worsley's. Lit 230. First class Collard and Collard, full compass ; cost £6O, for £l5. Lot 241, Powerful-tone Justin Browne Piano; worth £75, for 18 guineas. Lot 257. Excellent Piano, by Bord, Paris; cost £6O, for 18 guineas. Lot 260 to 281. A Grand Lot of Bargains, consisting of 21 Pianos, all second-hand, all good, and warranted; maker and juices only quoted to save space; 260 by Tomkinson, cost 1 £6O, for £7 10s. ; 261 by Broadwoed, cost £4O, for £2 15,.; 262 by Collard, cost £5O, lor £lO ; 263 by Oliver, cost £49, for , £7 15s. ; 264 by Ajello, cost £6O. for £l5; 265 by Bishop, for £l7 10s., worth £5O ; 266 by Ballingall, cost £45, for £6; 267 by Cadby, cost £5O, for £6 103. ;268 by Klrkmam, cost £7O, for £l2 10s. ; and the rest varying from 30s. to £lO 10s. All good Instruments.</p>
